course: dictionary
lesson: 403
title: Health words in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Appendicitis is a long word, but context helps. It is an illness in which the appendix, a small tube joined to the large intestine, becomes swollen and painful. The ending -itis is used for illnesses where a body part is swollen or sore.
explain: «Pain that starts round the belly button and moves to the bottom right side, with fever, can be appendicitis and needs a doctor.» The clues are pain, fever and needs a doctor. So appendicitis is a serious illness that a doctor must check quickly.
explain: «A girl in Dublin did not mention to the doctor that her tummy pain had moved to the lower right side; the next day it was much worse and it turned out to be appendicitis needing surgery.» Here the clues are much worse and surgery. The lesson is to tell a grown-up and a doctor when pain moves or gets worse.
fact: Appendicitis means an illness where the appendix becomes swollen and painful.
fact: The appendix is a small tube joined to the large intestine.
fact: Appendicitis usually needs an operation, called surgery.
fact: Pain that moves or gets worse, with fever, is a reason to see a doctor quickly.
fact: Phrases you may read: have appendicitis, and acute appendicitis, where acute means sudden and serious.
exercise: «Pain that starts round the belly button and moves to the bottom right side, with fever, can be appendicitis.» What is appendicitis? | A type of cold weather | Pain in the head after reading a long book | A kind of tasty pudding | *A swollen, painful appendix, a small tube joined to the large intestine
exercise: In the Dublin story, what did the girl's tummy pain do? | Went away completely | Stayed in the same place all day | Turned into a cold | *Moved to the lower right side
exercise: Which word in the Dublin sentence tells you the illness needed an operation? | *surgery | girl | tummy | Dublin
test: Ella reads, «She has acute appendicitis.» What does acute suggest? | Blue and cold | Slow and gentle | Very funny | *Sudden and serious
test: Which of these is the appendix? | A part of the brain | *A small tube joined to the large intestine | A large bone in the leg | A kind of sickness tablet
exam: Based on the sentences, what should a child with sharp, moving tummy pain and fever do? | Eat a big meal | Wait a week and say nothing | Keep it secret from grown-ups | *Tell a grown-up and get a doctor quickly
